A glob view prints a TOML file's header comment, or else a field summary: its first three scalar keys before the first table, then `...` if it has more.
Without scalar keys before the first table, the summary takes the first table's keys and names the table; without any scalar keys there is nothing to summarize.
== args
input
== file input/commented.toml
# Commented settings.
a = 1
== file input/rustfmt.toml
edition = "2024"
max_width = 100
== file input/many.toml
a = 1
b = 'two'
c = true
d = 1979-05-27
== file input/Cargo.toml
[package]
name = "demo"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2024"
[dependencies]
== file input/lists.toml
items = [1, 2]
[[bin]]
path = ["x"]
== stdout
glob view: input
input/Cargo.toml (5 lines): [package] {name = "demo", version = "0.1.0", edition = "2024"}
input/commented.toml (2 lines): Commented settings.
input/lists.toml (3 lines): (no header available)
input/many.toml (4 lines): {a = 1, b = 'two', c = true, ...}
input/rustfmt.toml (2 lines): {edition = "2024", max_width = 100}
== stderr
== exit 0
